                "sender": "w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov",
                "senderName": "NWS Tiyan GU",
                "headline": "Flash Flood Warning issued September 6 at 7:15PM ChST until September 6 at 8:45PM ChST by NWS Tiyan GU",
                "description": "FFWGUM\n\nThe National Weather Service in Tiyan has issued a\n\n* Flash Flood Warning for...\nSouthwestern Guam...\n\n* Until 845 PM ChST.\n\n* At 715 PM ChST, Doppler radar indicated heavy showers, with the\npotential for thunderstorms, producing heavy rain across the warned\narea. Between 2 and 3 inches of rain have fallen. Additional\nrainfall amounts of 1 to 3 inches are possible in the warned area.\nFlash flooding is ongoing or expected to begin shortly.\n\nHAZARD...Flash flooding caused by heavy showers and possible\nthunderstorms.\n\nSOURCE...Radar indicated.\n\nIMPACT...Flash flooding of small creeks and streams, urban areas,\nhighways and streets, as well as other poor drainage and\nlow-lying areas.",
                "instruction": "Turn around, don't drown when encountering flooded roads. Most flood\ndeaths occur in vehicles.\n\nBe aware of your surroundings and do not drive on flooded roads.\n\nReport flooding to law enforcement.\n\nPlease report observed flooding to local emergency services or law\nenforcement and request they pass this information to the National\nWeather Service when you can do so safely.",
                "response": "Avoid",
                "note": null,
